NAME
    term - a command line in a window (the video card V4)

SYNOPSIS
    term

DESCRIPTION
    A window on the graphics screen with a prompt. Type a command
    line (the video card's PS/2 keyboard) and press Enter: it runs,
    and what it printed comes back in the window, under the line.
    cd changes the folder of the next prompt; pipes work. clear
    empties the window. bye, Ctrl-Q or Quit in the menu bar ends
    term.

    What was typed and printed is kept in /term.log, so term shows
    it again when it starts.

NOTES
    A line runs through the script /term.sh, which term writes: the
    line with - before it (it may fail) and > /term.out after it,
    then term -r (which adds /term.out to the log and shows the
    window). The error messages come into the window too: term sets
    ERRTO (man sh) while the line runs. A program that asks for
    input asks with its question in the file. /term.log keeps its
    last 2,000 characters when it passes 4,000.
    Needs /lib/wmk. Written 2026-11-20 after the P8X's term.
